## 1. Purpose

This record is the approved, versioned configuration of {{tool_name}} at {{org_name}} (owner: {{role_tool_owner}}). It separates **configuration** (versionable, baselined, change-controlled: settings, permission rules, sandbox, hooks, MCP servers, instruction files, model envelope, code-host gates) from **behaviour** (variable: models can change without a version change, so behaviour is covered by monitoring, the model admission check MA-01 and periodic re-tests in {{doc_id_08}}).

The binding controls live server-side (code host and CI). The tool's local configuration is defence in depth and is recorded here so that drift can be detected.

Regulatory anchors:
{{#reg_iso13485}}
- ISO 13485:2016 clause 4.1.6 (validated state maintained after changes), clause 4.2.4 (agent configuration and instruction files are controlled items), clause 4.2.5 (records).
{{/reg_iso13485}}
{{#reg_fda_qmsr}}
- 21 CFR Part 820 (QMSR): 21 CFR 820.10, incorporating ISO 13485:2016 by reference (21 CFR 820.7). 21 CFR Part 11 applies to the records of this package that are kept or signed electronically.
{{/reg_fda_qmsr}}
{{#ctx_code_product}}
- IEC 62304: tools and settings used to develop the software are supporting items under configuration control (clauses 5.1.10 and 8.1).
{{/ctx_code_product}}
{{#reg_gxp}}
- EU GMP Annex 11 clause 10 (change and configuration management){{^reg_fda_qmsr}}; 21 CFR Part 11 for configuration records kept electronically{{/reg_fda_qmsr}}.
{{/reg_gxp}}

## 2. How to fill in this record

1. The {{role_tool_owner}} writes the **approved value** of every item before IQ-03.
2. The executor of IQ-03 captures the **effective value**:
{{#is_claude_code}}
   - run `python3 checks/capture_baseline.py --tool claude_code --repo <path-to-repo> --operator "<name>" --out evidence/{{tool_id}}/IQ-03/` on each reference machine and runner, and copy the values and file hashes from its output;
{{/is_claude_code}}
{{#is_codex}}
   - run `python3 checks/capture_baseline.py --tool codex --repo <path-to-repo> --operator "<name>" --out evidence/{{tool_id}}/IQ-03/` on each reference machine and runner, and copy the values and file hashes from its output;
{{/is_codex}}
{{#is_copilot}}
   - the capture script does not cover this tool: export or screenshot each setting below and hash every file;
{{/is_copilot}}
{{#is_cursor}}
   - the capture script does not cover this tool: export or screenshot each setting below and hash every file;
{{/is_cursor}}
{{#is_other}}
   - the capture script does not cover this tool: export or screenshot each setting below and hash every file;
{{/is_other}}
   - fill the manual fields (admin console, code host) from exports, or from dated screenshots when no export exists.
3. Mark each row Match / No match. A "No match" is a deviation in {{doc_id_05}}.
4. Any later change to an approved value follows {{doc_id_08}} and produces a new baseline revision; earlier revisions are kept.

